   "ruling": "Ruling: model error; Form 2441 line 3, \"If you completed Part III, enter the amount from line 31\"; i2441 p. 6, Line 26, \"If line 26 is more than zero, you have taxable dependent care benefits. Enter this amount on Form 1040, 1040-SR, or 1040-NR, line 1e\". executable-triage-v2 (rerun of triage.py's triage() with the witness cap lifted, record in scratch `/tmp/adj-bklg-dep-f2441/triage/f2441.json`; 1,495 fixtures, 500 generated returns seed 20261026, 380 partial records from 40 bases; 2,375 comparisons): 717 of 2,375 agree; 1,364 candidate-unknown, 264 candidate-refuses, 24 project-unknown, 5 project-refuses, 1 value; on completed returns: 196 candidate-unknown, 26 candidate-refuses. The expression (line 26 > 0) is the earlier reply's, but this reply's line 26 is no longer guarded by f2441.benefits: it evaluates Part III for every filer, so on returns that file no Part III it asks the Part III answers the interview never asks (f2441.line13 83, Form W-2 box 10 of every employer, f2441.plan_max, line14, paid_2026, employer_care, nondependent, student_disabled) and refuses f2441.plans_differ (25) where the project gives false. No value difference on a completed return; the 1 value is on a refused return. The project tests f1040.line1e, which copies line 26 only with benefits. Project stands.",
